cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or pipeline, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MarkSentry: Secure, Local-First Document-to-Markdown Conversion"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sunilgentyala/marksentry"
url: "https://sunilgentyala.github.io/marksentry/"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Gentyala
    given-names: Sunil
    affiliation: "HCLTech (HCL America Inc.), Dallas, TX, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2642-3479"
    email: sunil.gentyala@ieee.org
abstract: >
  MarkSentry is a local-first document-to-Markdown converter for PDF, DOCX,
  and ZIP inputs. It applies zero-trust input sanitization (path-traversal
  jailing, SSRF mitigation, VBA macro stripping, zip-bomb detection,
  magic-byte validation) before parsing, reconstructs multi-column PDF
  layouts and GFM tables, converts OMML/Unicode math to LaTeX, and offers
  optional PII masking for RAG ingestion pipelines. No network calls are
  made during conversion.
keywords:
  - document-conversion
  - markdown
  - pdf-to-markdown
  - docx
  - zero-trust
  - ssrf-protection
  - pii-masking
  - local-first
  - rag
  - latex
